      overview: "Trading is a commendable, Qur'an-sanctioned profession; the permissibility of trading precedes the prohibition of Riba in the Qur'an, signifying trade as the legitimate alternative, justified by risk-bearing under Al-Kharaj bi-al-Daman.",
      simpleExplanation: "Islam actively encourages trading and even the Prophet and his Companions traded for a living. The order of the Qur'anic verse -- mentioning that trade is allowed before saying interest is banned -- is read as pointing to trade as the proper alternative to interest. A trader's profit is fair because he does real work (finding, buying, storing, transporting goods) and takes on real risk (loss, damage, price swings); a lender earning interest does neither.",
