      overview: "Sales are classified by legal status (valid/Sahih, void/Batil, voidable/Fasid, suspended/Mawquf, as per Chapter 5) and by the nature of the counter-values exchanged (Bai' al-Sarf, Bai' al-Muqayaza, Mu'ajjal, Salam, Bai' al-Mutlaq, etc.).",
      simpleExplanation: "Sales can be sorted in two ways: by whether they're legally sound (fully valid, totally void, fixable/voidable, or on hold), and by what's being exchanged for what -- money for money, goods for goods (barter), goods now for money later (credit), or money now for goods later (Salam).",
